# Chrome closes the hidden Browser that holds a profile's pages, and the bridge's next page arrives after Chrome
# has scheduled that Browser's deletion. The page went into the closing Browser's tab strip, which was no longer
# empty when Chrome deleted it, after the window's features had gone: ExclusiveAccessManager::OnTabClosing on a
# null manager from ~Browser stopped Cra (three 0.1.44 crash reports from three Macs). HostFor now leaves a
# closing host to close and makes a new one (bridge.mm). Cra.debugCloseHost with addPage adds that page as Chrome
# finishes closing; without the change Chrome stops there instead (TabStripModel::InsertDetachedTabAt, checked 17 Nov).
budget rss=700
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://debug?cdp=Cra.debugCloseHost&params={"addPage":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Cra\.debugCloseHost → .*closing
wait 3
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=after-close
expect-log GET /page\.html\?n=after-close
wait 2
